    {
      "title": "Transforming Text with sed and awk",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transforming Text with sed and awk",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. sed: Line Edits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`s/old/new/g` replaces ==every match== on each line",
                "No `g`: only the **first** match per line changes",
                "Any delimiter works: `s|/usr|/opt|`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "sed option",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`-n '5,10p'`",
                  "prints **only** lines 5-10"
                ],
                [
                  "`/re/d`",
                  "deletes matching lines"
                ],
                [
                  "`-i`",
                  "edits the file ==in place=="
                ],
                [
                  "`-i.bak`",
                  "GNU: keeps a backup"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. awk: pattern { action }",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Runs per line: ==pattern== selects, `{ action }` runs",
                "`$1`..`$NF` fields, `$0` whole line, `NR` line number",
                "`-F,` sets the field separator",
                "`END` block runs once, after the last line"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "awk '$3 > 100 {print $1}' f",
                "awk '{s+=$2} END{print s}' f"
              ],
              "note": "filter then print; sum a column"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing the Tool",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Use for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`cut`",
                  "simple column pulls"
                ],
                [
                  "`sed`",
                  "line edits, substitution"
                ],
                [
                  "`awk`",
                  "per-field logic, conditions, arithmetic"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Forget `g` and only the first match per line changes. `-i` rewrites the file: use `-i.bak`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Building Pipelines with xargs and Avoiding Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Building Pipelines with xargs and Avoiding Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What xargs Does",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`xargs` turns stdin items into arguments; it splits on ==blanks and newlines==",
                "Needed because many commands ignore stdin",
                "`grep -l TODO *.c | xargs wc -l`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Safe Input and Flags",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`my file.log` becomes **two** arguments",
                "Fix: NUL-separated input with `-0`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "find . -name '*.log' -print0 | xargs -0 rm"
              ],
              "note": "-print0 pairs with -0"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`-n1`",
                  "one argument per call"
                ],
                [
                  "`-I{}`",
                  "places the argument anywhere: `xargs -I{} cp {} /backup`"
                ],
                [
                  "`-P4`",
                  "runs 4 jobs in parallel"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Exit Status and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pipeline status is that of the ==last command== only",
                "`set -o pipefail` makes a failing stage fail the pipeline"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Useless `cat file | grep x`: use `grep x file`",
                "`uniq` without `sort`",
                "Unquoted patterns",
                "`xargs rm` without previewing"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Preview first",
              "text": "Run `... | xargs echo rm`, check the list, then drop `echo`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
