          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `sort data.txt > data.txt`. What is in data.txt afterwards?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "==Empty==: the shell truncates the file before sort reads it",
                "Fix: `sort -o data.txt data.txt`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does `printf '10\\n2\\n10\\n' | sort | uniq -c` report?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Lexical sort gives 10, 10, 2, so the duplicates are adjacent",
                "Result: 10 counted 2 times, 2 counted 1 time"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With `cmd 2>&1 >f`, where do stdout and stderr go?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`2>&1` runs first, so stderr copies the terminal",
                "Then stdout goes to f: ==stdout in f, stderr on screen==",
                "Use `cmd >f 2>&1` to capture both"
              ]
            }
